# [How to Earn Discussion Marks]{color=blue}

@body

- Participate in icebreaker activities at the start of class.
- Engage in the class chat by responding to direct questions during the lecture.
- Provide thoughtful answers to open-ended questions about the material.
- Ask clarifying questions if something is unclear.
- Share personal experiences that relate to the course content.
- Post relevant news articles or resources that connect to the topics we discuss.
- Be on time for the Zoom meeting to earn discussion marks for punctuality.
- Adding emoji tags to another student's comment earns 0.1 points, up to 10 points.

=== layout: one-panel
hidden: true
# [Discussion Marks FAQ]{color=blue}

@body

- 1. Discussion Marks are mostly [based on the chat]{color=red}
  - Not all comments in the chat count, such as "hi", "thanks", or "yes"
  - You can earn up to 6 discussion marks from the chat
- 2. Answering Polls does NOT count
  - It is not easy for me to obtain that data
- 3. Being present in the Zoom meeting when class time starts
  - You can earn up to 2 discussion marks for [being on-time to class]{color=red}
- 4. Direct messages do not count

